              "content": "Role: Act as a Senior Machine Learning Engineer and Software Architect.\n\nContext: I am a software engineering student working on a final project called \"S-MAD\" (Single-Image Morphing Attack Detection). I have an empty current directory. I need you to scaffold the entire project structure and code base for me. The goal is to detect if a face is \"Bona Fide\" (Real) or \"Morphed\" (Fake).\n\nConstraints & Goals:\n\nSpeed & Simplicity: Use standard libraries (torch, torchvision, streamlit) and pre-trained models (Transfer Learning on ResNet50) to ensure we have a working baseline immediately.\n\nClean Architecture: The code must be modular. Separate the model logic, image preprocessing, and the UI.\n\nUI First: We need a Streamlit web interface to demonstrate the project.\n\nExecution Plan (Please execute these steps):\n\nStep 1: File Structure Setup Create the following directory structure:\n\ndata/raw (for dataset)\n\ndata/processed (for preprocessed tensors)\n\nmodels/checkpoints (to save .pth weights)\n\nsrc/ (core logic)\n\nnotebooks/ (for experimentation)\n\napp.py (entry point for the UI)\n\nrequirements.txt\n\nREADME.md\n\nStep 2: Dependencies Create a requirements.txt file containing: torch, torchvision, streamlit, opencv-python-headless, Pillow, numpy, scikit-learn, tqdm.\n\nStep 3: The Model Core (src/model.py) Write a Python script that defines a class MorphDetector.\n\nIt should load a pre-trained ResNet50 from torchvision.models.\n\nReplace the final fully connected layer to output 2 classes (Real vs. Morph).\n\nInclude a helper method load_weights(path) to load local weights safely.\n\nStep 4: Inference Logic (src/inference.py) Write a script with a function predict_image(model, image_path).\n\nIt should handle standard image preprocessing (Resize to 224x224, Normalize).\n\nIt should return the probability score and the label (\"Real\" or \"Morph\").\n\nStep 5: The Web UI (app.py) Create a streamlit app that:\n\nLoads the model (cache it using @st.cache_resource).\n\nAllows the user to upload a JPG/PNG.\n\nDisplays the image.\n\nspecific visual cues: If 'Morph' -> Red alert box; If 'Real' -> Green success box.\n\nCrucial: If no custom weights are found in models/checkpoints, the app should warn the user but still run using the default ImageNet weights (just for demo purposes).\n\nStep 6: Documentation Create a README.md explaining how to install requirements and run streamlit run app.py.\n\nAction: Generate all files and code now."
